{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "scope": "user",
  "platforms": [
    "linux"
  ],
  "name": "Media Control (MPRIS)",
  "description": "Control whatever is already playing on this machine -- a browser tab, a music player, a video player -- over MPRIS, the freedesktop D-Bus interface Linux media applications implement. See what is playing with title, artist, album, position and length; play, pause, toggle, stop, skip to the next or previous track, seek by a number of seconds, and set a player's volume. Handles several players at once and defaults to whichever is actually making sound. Use for 'pause the music', 'what is playing', 'skip this', 'go back thirty seconds', 'turn it down'. Entirely local: no account, no API key, and no network access.",
  "summary": "Play, pause, skip, seek and set volume on any local media player over MPRIS, and report what is playing. Entirely local -- no account, no API key, no network.",
  "keywords": [
    "audio",
    "dbus",
    "media",
    "mpris",
    "music",
    "next track",
    "pause",
    "play",
    "playback",
    "player",
    "podcast",
    "seek",
    "skip",
    "video",
    "volume"
  ],
  "homepage": "https://github.com/JarvisOSLinux/mcp-registry",
  "transports": [
    {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "python3",
      "args": [
        "server.py"
      ],
      "platforms": [
        "linux"
      ],
      "description": "MPRIS media-control MCP Server"
    }
  ],
  "source": {
    "type": "git",
    "url": "https://github.com/JarvisOSLinux/mcp-registry.git",
    "rev": "39c50b058996bdbcec7da0ea04e1a37691f7e4a1",
    "path": "servers/mpris"
  },
  "setupScript": "setup.sh",
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "list_players",
      "description": "List the media players running on this machine with their identity, playback status and whether they can be controlled",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "get_now_playing",
      "description": "Report the current track: title, artist, album, playback status, position and length in seconds, and volume",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "play",
      "description": "Start or resume playback on a local media player",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "pause",
      "description": "Pause playback, keeping the current position",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "play_pause",
      "description": "Toggle between playing and paused, as the keyboard play/pause key does",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "stop",
      "description": "Stop playback and return to the start of the track",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "next_track",
      "description": "Skip to the next track",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "previous_track",
      "description": "Go to the previous track",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "set_volume",
      "description": "Set one player's volume between 0.0 and 1.0; values above the user's own maximum are refused",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "seek",
      "description": "Move the playback position by a relative number of seconds; negative rewinds",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    }
  ],
  "configurableProperties": [],
  "trust": {
    "reviewReferences": [
      "https://specifications.freedesktop.org/mpris-spec/latest/",
      "https://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/Specifications/mpris-spec/",
      "https://github.com/JarvisOSLinux/mcp-registry/tree/main/servers/mpris"
    ],
    "checks": [
      "license: server code is first-party, under this repository's licence",
      "source: maintained in-tree at servers/mpris, pinned by commit",
      "dependencies: none in Python -- standard library only (json, os, shutil, subprocess, sys)",
      "runtime dependency: busctl (systemd); setup.sh fails if absent",
      "network: none. Communication is with the user's own D-Bus session bus over a unix socket",
      "credentials: none",
      "filesystem: no reads or writes beyond the interpreter's own imports",
      "scope: acts only on MPRIS players already running as this user"
    ],
    "notes": "First-party server maintained in this repository. MPRIS is a freedesktop specification, so this server is Linux-only by nature rather than by omission -- there is no macOS or Windows equivalent of this bus to port it to. Players implement only a subset of the spec, so optional properties (Shuffle, LoopStatus, DesktopEntry) are reported as unknown rather than treated as errors.",
    "securityNotes": "Entirely local. The server reaches the user's own session bus over a unix socket, makes no network call, stores nothing, and can act only on media players already running as that user. It cannot start a player, open a file, or reach anything outside the MPRIS interface.\n\nThe playback tools are classified safe rather than elevated. They change state, but the state is local, non-destructive and instantly reversible: the worst outcome of an unintended call is that music pauses or a track is skipped, which one further call undoes. Requiring confirmation for 'pause' would make the capability unusable by voice, which is its primary use. set_volume is the one with a physical-world consequence, so it is clamped to the MPRIS range 0.0-1.0 and refuses the overdrive values above 1.0 that some players accept -- a tool call cannot make the machine louder than the user's own maximum.\n\nget_now_playing returns track title, artist and album, which are authored by whoever produced the media -- for a browser tab, the web page. That is an injection surface: a crafted page can put arbitrary text in a media title. The server groups those fields under `track_metadata_untrusted` and the tool description says to treat them as data, never as instructions. It is classified safe on the same basis as brave_web_search, which returns far more attacker-controlled text; maintainers who would rather follow the #86 rule ('third-party-content read >= elevated') should raise this one tool, at the cost of a confirmation prompt on every 'what is playing?'."
  },
